+# Ladybird Android Port
 
-This directory contains the first Android platform bring-up for Ladybird. It is deliberately small and explicit:
+Experimental Android port of the Ladybird web browser engine (LibWeb/LibJS).
 
-- a native Android application targeting API 30 and 64-bit ABIs;
-- a JNI bridge that verifies Android platform detection and a Unix socketpair round-trip;
-- a browser-shaped activity with an address field reserved for the future engine connection;
-- a GitHub Actions job that builds and lints the bootstrap APK.
+## Status
 
-The APK produced at this stage is **not a browser**. It does not use Android WebView and it does not link LibWeb, LibJS, WebContent, or the Ladybird UI. The next engine milestone is to build the portable Ladybird libraries with the NDK, then add an Android WebView::Application/ViewImplementation pair and a framebuffer/input bridge.
+**Current**: WebContent rendering architecture complete, Material 3 UI ready, waiting for vcpkg manifest to link LibWeb/LibJS.
 
-## Local build
